{\pard\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut Chorus 1\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut Fall on your knees!\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut Oh hear the angel voices!\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut Oh night divine!\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut Oh night when Christ was born,\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut Oh night divine!\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut Oh night, oh night divine! \par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut Verse 1\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut O holy night!\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut The stars are brightly shining;\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut It is the night\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut Of the dear Savior's birth.\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut Long lay the world\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut In sin and error pining;\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut Till He appeared\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut And the soul felt its worth.\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut A thrill of hope,\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut The weary world rejoices;\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut For yonder breaks,\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut A new and glorious morn.\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut Fall on your knees, \par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut Verse 2\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut Led by the light\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut Of faith serenely beaming,\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut With glowing hearts\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut By His cradle we stand.\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut So led by light\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut Of a star sweetly gleaming,\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut Here came the wise men\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut From orient land.\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut The King of kings\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut Lay thus in lowly manger,\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut In all our trials\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut Born to be our Friend;\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut He knows our need\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut To our weakness is no stranger.\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut Behold your King\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut Before Him lowly bend;\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut Behold your King\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut Before Him lowly bend! \par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut Verse 3\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut Truly He taught us\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut To love one another,\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut His law is love\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut And His gospel is peace;\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut Chains shall He break\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut For the slave is our brother,\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut And in His name\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut All oppression shall cease.\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut Sweet hymns of joy\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut In grateful chorus raise we,\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut Let all within us\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut Praise His holy name.\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut Christ is the Lord\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut O praise His name forever.\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut His power and glory evermore proclaim;\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut His power and glory evermore proclaim.}
